From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mieczyslaw Nalewaj <namiltd@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 06:12:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: force netdev name from DT ethernet alias

Interface naming currently depends on registration order between
stmmac instances, which is non-deterministic when multiple probes
race at boot (e.g. two independent GMACs with no shared switch).
This causes eth0/eth1 to swap randomly across reboots on some
platforms.

Force the netdev name to match the "ethernetN" DT alias when one is
present. plat->bus_id cannot be used for this: stmmac_platform.c
falls back to a driver-global counter when of_alias_get_id() finds
no alias, so plat->bus_id is never negative and every stmmac netdev
would be forced, including boards with no alias at all. Re-read the
alias directly from the device's OF node instead, and only force the
name when it actually resolves. Fall back to the original
auto-numbering template if the forced name collides.

Signed-off-by: Mieczyslaw Nalewaj <namiltd@yahoo.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c | 20 +++++++++++++++++++-
 1 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
@@ -7529,6 +7529,7 @@
 {
 	struct net_device *ndev = NULL;
 	struct stmmac_priv *priv;
+	int alias_id;
 	u32 rxq;
 	int i, ret = 0;
 
@@ -7783,7 +7784,24 @@
 		goto error_phy_setup;
 	}
 
-	ret = register_netdev(ndev);
+	/* Force name from DT alias instead of registration order,
+	 * which is non-deterministic across reboots.
+	 */
+	alias_id = of_alias_get_id(dev_of_node(priv->device), "ethernet");
+	if (alias_id >= 0) {
+		char orig_name[IFNAMSIZ];
+
+		strscpy(orig_name, ndev->name, IFNAMSIZ);
+		scnprintf(ndev->name, IFNAMSIZ, "eth%d", alias_id);
+		ret = register_netdev(ndev);
+		if (ret == -EEXIST) {
+			/* Name taken, fall back to auto-numbering */
+			strscpy(ndev->name, orig_name, IFNAMSIZ);
+			ret = register_netdev(ndev);
+		}
+	} else {
+		ret = register_netdev(ndev);
+	}
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(priv->device, "%s: ERROR %i registering the device\n",
 			__func__, ret);
